## 5. Environment Variables

Store all environment variables in `.env`. Commit `.env.example` with all keys present but no values. **Never commit `.env`.**

When reading `process.env` values with a fallback, always use `||` not `??`. A key that exists but is blank in `.env` (e.g. `PORT=`) passes through `??` as an empty string; `||` catches it and applies the default.

